+
+## T-009 completion evidence
+
+Complete Phase 1 code review, source/runtime identities, original failures and resolved findings, actual checks/QC, milestone TODO aggregation and exit assessment are in the [phase report](reports/phases/1/PHASE-REPORT.md). Scoped runtime assistance added explicit `-B` only to existing Python child argv in tests/checker; no semantic or governing amendment. After correcting the consumer quoting defect, 23 unit/18 integration tests, 36 isolated extracted module cases and every runnable user-guide fence pass on Python 3.12.14 with bytecode disabled. Initial failed runs remain retained. T-001–T-008 closing commits individually contain one initial owning checkbox plus result/evidence. Current fork tracking is explicitly disabled; copied hosted identities are protected and no issue/milestone write is made.
+
+This concrete T-009 report/checklist/result candidate awaits coordinator acceptance before the owning commit, immediate trial phase publication/readback, and two-parent local main integration/merged checks/trial main publication. Status in the proposed candidate reflects verified task and parent exits; durable completion and integration are not asserted before their actual operations. Phase 2 is eligible only afterward for selected T-010; T-011 onward and Phase 2 main integration are outside scope.
